  "initial_findings": "C-clean indexed callback trace1222 versus initialRust21 exposed copy/clear/put/result order. New native field arguments exposed guard coercion errors. Private C native function field access leaked76bytes while C target was clean. New release observers require scope-long receivers and repeated-loop replacement. A rotating fixture that clears a nonnil unrelated field leaves a stale C slot, and nil.length dereferencesNULL; these C failures are retained and excluded, replaced in new Python fixtures by defined nil-clear and nil-comparison controls. No original SN or oracle edited.",
  "separate_open_gap": "Computed call receiver field stores are still rejected by Rust; exploratory C implementation evaluates owned receiver three times and leaks aliases. No parity credit for that C-failing probe. Broader native/SDK/interface/generic/callback/lifecycle and final corpus/mode/platform goal remains open.",
